Acceptance criteria:
The original GBA startup and empty/loading screen have visible scanlines,
subtle RGB phosphor texture and edge shading. DS built-in status LCDs use
the same bounded treatment at their own row density. Native framebuffer
handoff replaces the entire placeholder: no host CRT overlay, shader pass,
pixel readback or per-game-frame processing. All nine actual native presets
and Unfiltered remain authoritative and unchanged. Cache tiny patterns and
gradients across startup frames; idle canvases do not animate or repaint
for this effect. Preserve full resolution, materials, lights, native
deadlines, retries0 and the complete deployment gate.

